WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.149
Here's how EdgeCoder works.

2
00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:04.740
Five things to know.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.110
First, you ask.

4
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:11.674
In a chat, a Code task, a bot, or through the API.

5
00:00:12.674 --> 00:00:15.869
Next, the coordinator picks the best fit.

6
00:00:15.869 --> 00:00:19.375
It matches your job to a model and a machine.

7
00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:22.044
Then a machine runs it.

8
00:00:22.044 --> 00:00:24.003
Your own machines are free.

9
00:00:24.003 --> 00:00:26.543
A host's machine is paid per token.

10
00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:31.609
Jobs travel encrypted between the coordinator and the machine.

11
00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:36.331
It's not end to end: the coordinator can read a job, so it can route it.

12
00:00:36.331 --> 00:00:38.495
Work on this computer stays here.

13
00:00:39.495 --> 00:00:42.879
Network calls cost cSats per token.

14
00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:44.813
One cSat is one sat.

15
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:46.940
Hosts keep 95 percent.

16
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.155
Also in EdgeCoder: bots run on a schedule, with a daily budget.

17
00:00:53.155 --> 00:00:54.440
Code is an agent.

18
00:00:54.440 --> 00:01:00.262
It edits your project, runs tests, and opens pull requests when you allow it.

19
00:01:01.262 --> 00:01:03.915
Tentacles are helpers on cheap models.

20
00:01:03.915 --> 00:01:06.569
They take parts of a big task at once.

21
00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:11.969
And type /remote in edgecoder code to carry on in the app.

22
00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:13.816
That's it.

23
00:01:13.816 --> 00:01:16.779
Press Next to set up this computer.
